BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC State African American Cultural Center
DTSTAMP:20260712T033929Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53391524798531
DTSTART:20260817T130000Z
DTEND:20260817T210000Z
DESCRIPTION:The Before We Knew Better art exhibition brings together the wo
 rk of Lamar Whidbee and Chris Facey to reflect on joy\, memory and the exp
 eriences that shape us early in life. The exhibition looks to childhood as
  a place of imagination\, play and connection. Rather than seeing nostalgi
 a as a way to escape the present\, the exhibition consider how memories of
  joy can remind us of what still matters. Whidbee and Facey ask what we ca
 rry with us from those early years and how those experiences continue to i
 nfluence our well-being\, relationships and sense of self.\n\nAt a time wh
 en conversations around mental health are increasingly important\, the exh
 ibition offers space to pause\, reflect and reconnect with the moments tha
 t first taught us about joy.
GEO:35.785108;-78.674529
LOCATION:Witherspoon Student Center\, 218
SUMMARY:Before We Knew Better Art Exhibition
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.ncsu.edu/event/before-we-knew-better-art-exh
 ibition
CATEGORIES:Exhibitions
END:VEVENT
