X-SOURCE:NC State African American Cultural Center
DTSTAMP:20260712T033929Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53374358673631
DTSTART:20260917T213000Z
DTEND:20260917T233000Z
DESCRIPTION:Join the African American Cultural Center (AACC) for the EQUIP 
 orientation and to learn how this year-long initiative can help you create
  the college experience you want in and outside of the classroom. EQUIP st
 ands for Empower\, Question\, Understand\, Initiate and Partner. The initi
 ative is designed to help first-year students:\n\nEmpower themselves to cr
 eate the college experience they want.Question everything to build habits 
 for life-long learning.Understand themselves and what they need to be succ
 essful.Initiate action and be proactive to find resources.Partner with oth
 ers to build a network of care and community.As an EQUIP participant\, you
  will:\n\nEngage in monthly check-ins with a dedicated staff member.Attend
  learning labs and AACC signature events.Work with an embedded AACC counse
 lor.Attend EQUIP special programs.Develop skills in self-awareness\, resil
 ience and help-seeking.EQUIP supports first-year students at NC State in c
 ultivating self-awareness\, community and resilience through AACC signatur
 e events\, wellness activities and proactive campus resource engagement.\n
 \nContact Andaiye Qaasim\, assistant director of the AACC\, at aaqaasim@nc
 su.edu if you have questions.
GEO:35.785108;-78.674529
LOCATION:Witherspoon Student Center\, African American Cultural Center Room
  356
SUMMARY:EQUIP Leadership Program Orientation for First-Year Students
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.ncsu.edu/event/equip-leadership-program-for-
 first-year-students
CATEGORIES:Student Life
CATEGORIES:Information Session
CATEGORIES:High-Impact Experiences
