BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:NC State African American Cultural Center
DTSTAMP:20260712T033929Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53374475146832
DTSTART:20260924T213000Z
DTEND:20260924T233000Z
DESCRIPTION:Are you ready to thrive at NC State? If so\, join the African A
 merican Cultural Center (AACC) for the EQUIP fall academic workshop. The w
 orkshop is designed to help first-year students master the academic transi
 tion to NC State. Co-facilitated with campus partners and peer leaders\, t
 his interactive session will focus on practical skills\, such as college-l
 evel study strategies\, major exploration\, syllabus navigation and buildi
 ng effective relationships with faculty and advisors. \n\nEQUIP is a year-
 long initiative that supports first-year students as they cultivate self-a
 wareness\, resilience\, and community. Through EQUIP\, you will:\n\nEmpowe
 r yourself to own your academic and personal journey.Question and develop 
 lifelong learning habits.Understand your strengths and what drives your su
 ccess.Initiate proactive connections with campus resources.Partner with pe
 ers and mentors to build a network of care.Participants will have access t
 o dedicated staff check-ins\, an embedded AACC counselor and exclusive spe
 cial events designed just for them.\n\nContact Andaiye Qaasim\, assistant 
 director of the AACC\, at aaqaasim@ncsu.edu if you have questions.
GEO:35.785108;-78.674529
LOCATION:Witherspoon Student Center\, African American Cultural Center (Roo
 m 356)
SUMMARY:EQUIP Academic Workshop
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.ncsu.edu/event/equip-academic-workshop
CATEGORIES:Workshops and Training
CATEGORIES:Student Life
CATEGORIES:High-Impact Experiences
END:VEVENT
